<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  A Dog Said... Animal Prosthetics 2 (SamBucher.ADogSaidAnimalProsthetics2, Workshop 3238353862).

  ADS 2 does not read RaceProperties or a body type to decide which animals get surgery. It keeps three
  abstract RecipeDefs, ADS_Cat1 (medieval replacements), ADS_Cat2 (+ simple prosthetics) and ADS_Cat3
  (+ bionics), each with a hand-curated <recipeUsers> list, and copies those lists onto the real surgery
  recipes in its own last patch. An animal absent from all three lists offers only amputation and
  euthanasia, as if the mod were not installed. Megabee is not listed, so without this file ADS 2 is a
  silent no-op for it.

  Megabee goes into all three categories. The choice follows its own vanilla-analogue references, not an
  intuition: its life-stage sounds are copied from Pawn_Megascarab_* (megabee.xml, <soundWounded> etc.)
  and its meat is Megaspider's (<useMeatFrom>Megaspider</useMeatFrom>). Both Megascarab and Megaspider are
  in ADS 2's own list (1.6/Defs/AnimalCategories/Animal_Categories.xml, read 2026-09-28) in Cat1, Cat2 and
  Cat3. The lists are cumulative, so an animal in Cat3 appears in the other two: all three additions are
  needed.

  The guard is PatchOperationConditional on ADS_Cat1. Without ADS 2 the xpath selects nothing, no
  <nomatch> is declared, and the operation reports success without logging anything. It is NOT MayRequire:
  MayRequire on an <Operation> is read by nothing (Verse.PatchOperation has no such field), so the
  operation would apply whether ADS 2 is loaded or not. Every branch of the predicate repeats @Name=, since
  [@Name="A" or "B"] is true for every RecipeDef in the document.

  About.xml declares <loadBefore>SamBucher.ADogSaidAnimalProsthetics2</loadBefore>: ADS 2 copies the lists
  once, at its own patch, so this patch has to run first or it writes into lists nobody reads any more.
-->
<Patch>

	<Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
		<xpath>/Defs/RecipeDef[@Name="ADS_Cat1"]</xpath>
		<match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
			<xpath>/Defs/RecipeDef[
				@Name="ADS_Cat3" or
				@Name="ADS_Cat2" or
				@Name="ADS_Cat1"
			]/recipeUsers</xpath>
			<value>
				<li>Megabee</li>
			</value>
		</match>
	</Operation>

</Patch>
